From 8b163d8583ea87cbaa07c2bad2f9c015f746d1b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:16:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] i386: add the KNC ISA and -march=knc

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: the Knights Corner (k1om) scalar ISA.

 - -mknc (OPTION_MASK_ISA2_KNC), "knc" in the -march table and
   --with-arch/--with-cpu, and the target("knc") attribute; __KNC__,
   __k1om and __k1om__ are predefined.
 - KNC is a P54C-derived in-order core: PROCESSOR_PENTIUM tuning with
   its own cost table (vector-unit stores and moves to the integer unit
   are priced out), no CMOV, no inter-unit moves, no CMPXCHG16B, no
   SAHF, no SSE/MMX; x86-64 only (the ISA bit is dropped for -m32).
   The __i586__/__pentium__ macros are not defined for 64-bit.
 - Scalar floating point stays on x87 (no fp movcc, no SSE compares),
   ffs<mode>2 is not used (it expands to cmov).
 - mfence is "lock or" on the stack; ldmxcsr/stmxcsr (the vector unit
   has an MXCSR) and their builtins are available.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
---
 gcc/common/config/i386/i386-common.cc |   2 +
 gcc/config.gcc                        |   2 +-
 gcc/config/i386/i386-builtins.cc      |   8 +-
